msgid "Contribute"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:9
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"We are happy to see you contribute to Zammad! You can do this in several "
"ways. Contributions are mainly done by forking one of our repos on GitHub "
"and creating a pull request with your changes (except for translations, see "
"below). 🚀"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid "You can contribute to:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "[Source-code](contribute#zammad-source-code)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "[Documentation](contribute#documentation)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "[Translation](contribute#translation)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Please have a look at our the sections below about how to contribute. All "
"repos can be found on [Github](https://github.com/zammad){target=_blank}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Zammad Source Code"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The Zammad source code can be found on GitHub in the [Zammad "
"repository](https://github.com/zammad/zammad){target=_blank}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Have a look at the [developer "
"manual](https://github.com/zammad/zammad/blob/develop/doc/developer_manual/index.md){target=_blank} "
"to get started."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:28
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Supported Branches / Versions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The main [Zammad "
"repository](https://github.com/zammad/zammad){target=_blank} at Github has "
"several branches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:32
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`develop`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This is the current (unreleased) development state of next major release "
"(this will become the new `stable` branch)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:38 src/en/contribute/contribute.md:51
#, markdown-text
msgid "Don't use it for production!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:38 src/en/contribute/contribute.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This branch is actively supported and receives regular bug fixes as well as "
"security updates (see [Security "
"Policy](https://github.com/zammad/zammad/blob/develop/SECURITY.md){target=_blank} "
"for more details)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:39
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`stable`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid "This is the current stable release, e.g. Zammad 5.2."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid "Use this branch for production installations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:46
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`stable-x.y`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:51
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"These are the branches of old versions of Zammad like `stable-5.1` for "
"Zammad 5.1."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:51
#, markdown-text
msgid "Bug fixes and security updates are not applied to these branches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: hero actions text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:52 src/en/contribute/contribute.md:95
#: src/en/documentation/index.md:1 src/en/index.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Documentation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "Do you want to contribute to the Zammad documentation?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:59
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Open a new GitHub pull request at <https://github.com/zammad/zammad-org> "
"(targeting the `develop` branch) with your changes and make sure to follow "
"the [style and content guide](style-guide). Consider to have a look at the "
"[repo's "
"README.md](https://github.com/zammad/zammad-org?tab=readme-ov-file#zammad-hub){target=_blank} "
"too."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:64
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The documentation you are reading is available on zammad.org and "
"next.zammad.org and is built with Vitepress. The source files are written in "
"Markdown. Make sure to change the English source files only which are placed "
"under `/src/en/`. The translation is done via Weblate and will overwrite any "
"changes in the language specific folders (except `/src/en/`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:65
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Translation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:70
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you want to help us with translation and improve the multi-language "
"support of Zammad and/or the documentation, you are welcome to contribute as "
"well! The translation of Zammad itself and the documentation is done by "
"using Weblate, which is a service for the collaborative translation of "
"projects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:73
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You just have to head over to Zammad's [Weblate "
"instance](https://translations.zammad.org/){target=_blank}.  You can either "
"create an account (if you don't have one already) or even sign in with your "
"Github account!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:78
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"We will cover some basic steps in the following sections to get you started "
"with translating. However, if you want to use some additional features of "
"Weblate and want to dive deeper into it, their [translation "
"documentation](https://docs.weblate.org/en/latest/user/translating.htm){target=_blank} "
"is a good starting point."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:79 src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:51
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:8
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Basics"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:83
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The translation of **Zammad** and the translation of the **documentation** "
"are split into different projects in Weblate.\n"
"When you click in the top menu under \"_Projects > Browse all projects_\", "
"you can find the overview of the projects:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:85
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot showing translation projects in Weblate and "
"menu](/screenshots/weblate-overview-docs.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:87
#, markdown-text
msgid "Structure of translation projects in Weblate:"
msgstr ""

