#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Zammad"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid "Zammad (`develop`, development version)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid "Zammad (`stable` version)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid "_Some more which aren't relevant here_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:96
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"It should be no big difference which branch you choose to translate. When "
"Weblate detects the same strings in different\n"
"branches, they will be used for all branches and only have to be translated "
"once. If in doubt, choose the `develop`\n"
"version.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:106
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After selecting a project (Documentation or Zammad), you will see different "
"sub-projects and their translation status summarized for all "
"languages. These overviews may show a quite low translation rate, which is "
"due to the amount of active languages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:110
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here you can select one of the \"components\", which is more or less the "
"same as different versions. After selecting one\n"
"of them, you can see the status of translation for the different languages, "
"as you can see in the following screenshot\n"
"with an example from _Documentation > User Documentation (latest)_:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:112
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot showing translation status of different languages for the user "
"documentation](/screenshots/weblate-translations-user-docs.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:113
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Translating"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:117
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After selecting your language you want to translate to, a good starting "
"point is to select \"_Untranslated strings_\" (or the same meaning in your "
"language, depending on what you have set in your profile)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:120
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After that, you will finally see the first untranslated string in the upper "
"field and, in theory, you can start to translate. First a brief overview of "
"the user interface of Weblate:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:122
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot of Weblate translation user "
"interface](/screenshots/weblate-ui.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:136
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Breadcrumbs with path** to the current project and language"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:136
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Translation area** itself. You can find the source string (_\"English "
"(United States)\"_) at the top and the field for your translation "
"(_\"French\"_ in this example)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:136
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Glossary**: here you can find common translations in Zammad context. The "
"terms from the glossary are highlighted in the source strings, as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:136
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Some useful tabs**:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:136
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Nearby strings**: shows you the context of the word or string"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:136
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Automatic suggestions**: here you can find automatic suggestions from "
"DeepL and suggestions from similar strings, which are already "
"translated. Use the \"_Clone to translation_\" button to insert it in the "
"translation field to apply changes. Use the \"_Accept_\" button to accept "
"the suggested translation and automatically switch to the next string."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:136
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Other languages**: here you can get an overview, which languages are "
"translated and you can also see the translated strings (could be useful for "
"languages, which are similar)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:137
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:107
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:553
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:142
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"And finally some examples for \"special\" source strings, you might see in "
"the documentation projects. You should also have a look at the [style "
"guide](style-guide) where you can find more information about the syntax and "
"the usage of Markdown/Vitepress features."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:146
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**\\`example-string\\`**\n"
": This is rendered as `example-string`. Depending on the context, it can be "
"translated or not. In any case, use the\n"
"  \\` before and after the string in your translation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:152
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**\\[example\\](/en/path/to/document-or-website\\)**\n"
": This is a link to another page, including the language code. The above "
"\"example\" is the text, which is shown as\n"
"  link text. This part can be translated. For the path, only the `en` may be "
"replaced by the language code you are\n"
"  translating in. Make sure that your language is already present on "
"zammad.org (check it by using the language\n"
"  switcher). Otherwise contact us if you want to have your language "
"activated.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:155
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**\\*\\*example string\\*\\***\n"
": Markup for text (e.g. bold, italics). Alternative: \\_example "
"string\\_. These strings can be translated, but the\n"
"  markup (e.g. `**` or `_`) should be adopted true to meaning.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Style and Content Guide"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:9
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This guide provides an overview of the content that should be included in "
"the Zammad documentation, as well as formatting and style guidelines to "
"ensure clarity and readability."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The first sections are about general information and rules. A [section with "
"examples](#examples) follows at the end."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you have questions, feel free to ask in our community. If you want to "
"contribute, you may also want to have a look at our [contribution "
"page](contribute) or [ask in an "
"issue](https://github.com/zammad/zammad-org/issues){target=_blank} to get "
"started."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:16
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Audience Assumptions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The documentation is written assuming that **users** have a basic "
"understanding of web browser usage and common software design concepts. This "
"means for example that features are described in detail, but not on a level "
"of how to open a dropdown field."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The **Zammad administrator** additionally should have a basic technical "
"understanding and should also know the workflows and communication processes "
"in its company."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For self-hosted instances, **system administrators** should also be familiar "
"with Linux system administration basics.  Access to the host system "
"(e.g. via SSH) and administrative permissions are taken for granted for "
"system administrators."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:28
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Content"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "The documentation aims to include information about:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "How to use Zammad"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"How to manage Zammad as an admin (e.g. setting it up after installation, "
"adjust settings, configure features)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Different ways how to install Zammad"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Additional guides if (host) system configuration and/or configuration of "
"third party systems is needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Regarding the **level of detail**, the [audience "
"assumptions](#audience-assumptions) should be considered. Because one of the "
"goals of Zammad is to be intuitive and user friendly, there is no need to "
"describe each click in detail. However, important steps should be "
"included. The readers should achieve their goals as quickly and easily as "
"possible without having to read a lot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Due to the fact that a documentation can't cover everything (otherwise it "
"would be on a code-like detail level), the relevance has to be "
"considered. If parts with a common use case are missing, it should be "
"intended to include them in the documentation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:46
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Style and Rules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The next sections cover general things to consider writing the "
"documentation. After these you can find a section with some "
"[examples](#examples) about how to format and structure the content."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The documentation is written in the Markdown markup language. The source "
"files have the extension `.md`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The system uses [Vitepress](https://vitepress.dev/){target=_blank} to build "
"the website."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid "The language of the source files is American English."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
