#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Style"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid "Use short and clear sentences and prioritize information over complexity."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Page title and headings: capitalize the first letter of all words except "
"minor words (see [title "
"case](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Title_case){target=_blank})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use breadcrumb separation for paths and locations with `>` as separator and "
"format path in italics, e.g.  _Settings > Channels > Chat_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid "Use code highlighting to emphasize programming snippets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid "Use [info, tip, warning and danger boxes](#custom-boxes) when needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use a [detail box](#custom-boxes) when content may not be relevant for all "
"the readers or may break the reading flow otherwise."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If available, use icons for important UI buttons like ::+:: and ::x:: (see "
"[examples](#text-and-ui) below)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Include screenshots when necessary. The preferred way of adding screenshots "
"of Zammad is by creating them automatically [using "
"Cypress](https://github.com/zammad/zammad-org?tab=readme-ov-file#automatic-screenshots-cypress){target=_blank}.  "
"This supports the maintainability of the documentation because the "
"screenshots are re-generated each time the build pipeline runs. Please note "
"that the usage of Cypress is not part of this documentation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid "Provide step-by-step instructions with clear explanations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid "Use examples or scenarios to illustrate concepts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid "Include relevant images or diagrams when necessary."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Spell abbreviations full the first time they are used or include them in the "
"glossary and link to them. Broadly used and common abbreviations may be "
"excluded from this rule."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid "If in doubt, align it to the existing documentation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:83
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Conventions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:89
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The documentation stack includes automated checks (linting) to ensure "
"compliance with the style guide and common rules for Markdown files. To "
"check if your changes are compliant, run `pnpm lint` to perform the "
"check. Some of the recognized problems can be even fixed automatically by "
"running `pnpm lint:fix`. Make sure to run the check before committing your "
"changes. Otherwise the build of the documentation will fail."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:93
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The used linting has some built in rules which you can find "
"[here](https://github.com/DavidAnson/markdownlint/blob/v0.32.1/README.md#rules--aliases){target=_blank}. "
"Some important rules and customized ones are mentioned below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:108
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Line length of 120 characters in the source file may not be exceeded for "
"standard text. Make sure to use a line break before reaching this limit. A "
"visual indicator in your editor may be helpful. This does not apply for "
"special content like paths to screenshots and long links."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:108
#, markdown-text
msgid "Multiple consecutive empty lines are not allowed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:108
#, markdown-text
msgid "Empty lines before and after headings and fenced code blocks are required."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:108
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use `` ``` `` (backticks) for fenced code blocks, followed by a mandatory "
"language tag, e.g. `ruby` or `sh`. If no language is applicable, use "
"`plain`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:108
#, markdown-text
msgid "Use `-` for bullet point lists (unordered lists) like this one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:108
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To easily distinguish between **bold** and _italics_, use `_` around the "
"text for italics and `**` for bold (e.g.  `_italic_` vs. `**bold**`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:108
#, markdown-text
msgid "Multiple headings with the same content are not allowed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:108
#, markdown-text
msgid "Each document must have exactly one `h1` heading as title."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:108
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Resolution of manual full page screenshots for _mobile view_ is 400x867 "
"pixels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:108
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Resolution of manual full page screenshots for _desktop view_ is 1920x1080 "
"pixels."
msgstr ""

