#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:111
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Text and UI"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:122
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Type                      | Highlighting in documentation | Markdown "
"syntax                 |\n"
"|-------------------------- "
"|-------------------------------|---------------------------------|\n"
"| Labeled buttons           | `Sign in`                     | \\`Sign in\\`                     "
"|\n"
"| Fields and UI elements    | **Name**                      | "
"\\*\\*Name\\*\\*                    |\n"
"| Locations/paths           | _Settings > Channels > Email_ | \\_Settings > "
"Channels > Email\\_ |\n"
"| Keyboard shortcuts        | [[x]]                         | \\[\\[x\\]\\]                       "
"|\n"
"| Add button                | ::+::                         | "
"\\:\\:\\+\\:\\:                      |\n"
"| Delete button             | ::x::                         | \\:\\:x\\:\\:                       "
"|\n"
"| Action menu               | ::a::                         | \\:\\:a\\:\\:                       "
"|\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:123
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Heading Structure"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/style-guide.md:127
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Every documentation file must include exactly one title on top level (like "
"`# Title`). Levels below should always contain at least two sections. If "
"only one section exists, consider merging it with the higher-level content."
msgstr ""

