msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:17
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:43
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:65
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:82
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:97
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:119
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:137
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:175
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:187
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:209
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:236
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:268
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:293
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:310
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:327
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Why?**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"It is possible to automatically close a ticket tab in the navigation "
"sidebar. It depends on your preferences, but you can save a click after "
"updating or updating a ticket to _closed_ state."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:22
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:50
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:70
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:87
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:104
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:125
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:144
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:180
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:195
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:219
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:240
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:276
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:298
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:315
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:333
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**How?**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In the footer bar of the ticket detail view, click on the `Stay on tab ^` "
"button and select your desired option (if the default is still set, "
"otherwise it is labeled as the other options below). You have different "
"options:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Stay on tab**: Default option. You have to manually close the tab if you "
"want to have it removed from your navigation sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Close tab**: This option closes the tab on each update of the "
"ticket. Might be a good option if you have to deal with many tickets and/or "
"the tickets require many interactions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Close tab on ticket close**: This option only closes the tab when the "
"ticket is updated and the state is set to _closed_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:33
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If your situation differs from ticket to ticket, you can leave **Stay on "
"tab** and use the keyboard shortcut\n"
"[[Shift]] [[c]] for changing the ticket state to closed and close the ticket "
"tab.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Text Modules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows text modules "
"feature](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/ticket-article-text-template.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid "The usage of text modules has benefits like:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "You save time while answering tickets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Answers from you and your colleagues are aligned because you use the same "
"text for answers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To use text modules simply type `::` in the editor followed by parts of the "
"name or keyword of the text module."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can pick one by clicking on it or by using the up and down arrows "
"followed by [[Enter]] on your keyboard. There are some text modules in "
"Zammad which are shipped by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:59
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you have to answer the same question again and again, ask your Zammad "
"admin to create such a text module for you.  They can even include variables "
"like customer name or any other available attribute which get replaced while "
"using it in a ticket."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:60
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Mention a Colleague"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:63
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows mention "
"feature](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/ticket-article-mention.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:68
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Ask or request information from your colleagues or mention them in important "
"tickets so they receive notifications for ticket updates and are "
"automatically subscribed to this ticket."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:73
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"While writing a ticket article, simply type `@@` and enter some letters of "
"the name of the colleague you want to mention."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:76
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad displays a list with all possible matches where you can pick one by "
"clicking on it or by using the up and down arrows followed by [[enter]] on "
"your keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:77
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Subscribe to a Ticket"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:80
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows subscribe "
"feature](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/ticket-subscribe.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:85
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you are interested in the progress of a ticket, you are not the owner, "
"you can subscribe to it. This means you will receive notifications for each "
"update."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:91
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Activate the \"Subscribe me\" toggle in the ticket side panel to get "
"notifications. If you have been mentioned in a ticket, you are automatically "
"subscribed. Switch the toggle off to stop the notification. The avatars "
"displayed show you who has subscribed to the ticket and is therefore "
"notified of updates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:92
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:158
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Macros"
msgstr ""

