#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:291
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows the article action split "
"menu](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/ticket-split.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:296
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you have a ticket which is about more than one issue, you might want to "
"split it in two or more separate tickets.  For example this might be the "
"case if a customer has a technical question and wants to place an order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:300
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To split an article off, use the ::a:: menu next to an article and select "
"`Split`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:303
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This results in a ticket create screen with the same attributes set as in "
"the initial ticket. The content of the article is also included. You can "
"change everything to your needs and then click on `Create`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:306
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The just created ticket is linked in the original one as child. The original "
"ticket is linked in the split off ticket as parent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:307
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Link Tickets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:313
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"When tickets about related issues arise, they can be linked to each other "
"for easier reference.  [Merged](#merge-tickets) and [split](#split-tickets) "
"tickets are automatically linked."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:319
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In the ticket sidebar, add a link to another ticket by clicking the ::+:: "
"button in the \"Links\" section. This opens a side panel in which you can "
"select a ticket by clicking on it or enter a ticket number in search "
"field. Additionally, you can choose between different link types:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:323
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Normal:** for related ticket which have no hierarchy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:323
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Parent/Child**: for related tickets where one is the main issue and the "
"other is a subtask. This link type is used by default if a tickets gets "
"split or merged."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:324
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/time-accounting.md:1
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/time-accounting.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Time Accounting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:331
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"With Zammad's integrated time accounting, you can help to keep track of how "
"much time you spent on tickets. Based on the accounted times in the ticket, "
"it is automatically assigned to customers and organizations. This might be "
"used in your company for billing or to keep track of support budgets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:335
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After updating a ticket, a time accounting dialog will appear. Enter how "
"much time you spent on the ticket."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:337
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows the time accounting "
"dialog](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/time-accounting-dialog.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:340
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The feature is **optional**. If you don't see it whenever you update a "
"ticket, your administrator hasn't enabled it yet or the rule for tickets to "
"be taken into consideration doesn't match."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:343
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The accounted time is always recorded and stored without a unit. However, "
"your administrator may decide to show an optional label next to the field to "
"hint you and your colleagues in which unit the time is expected (see "
"screenshot)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:346
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Activity types can be used to distinguish between different activities and "
"for grouping the accounted times. If this optional feature is active, it "
"shows a list of activities from which you can select in the time accounting "
"dialog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:350
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If a ticket already has accounted time(s), you can see it in the ticket "
"sidebar on the right side in the ticket detail view at the bottom. You can "
"find the calculated sums of each activity type (if configured) as well as "
"the total sum of accounted times for all activity types."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:351
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows the time accounting "
"overview](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/time-accounting-overview.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:1 src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "FAQs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details How to find tickets?)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It depends on your use case. Zammad offers many possibilities to search and "
"access tickets.\n"
"\n"
"If you **search for a specific ticket or content**, the search is the best "
"way. You can find the search field in the top\n"
"area of the navigation sidebar or activate it by using the keyboard shortcut "
"[[s]]. The search even shows your\n"
"last viewed items, maybe you can find what you are searching for already "
"there. There is a separate\n"
"[search page](./guides/search) for more information.\n"
"\n"
"If you want to **start working on tickets**, take a look at [the "
"overviews](./guides/overviews), which are basically a\n"
"list of current tickets. These overviews should put you in a position where "
"you can easily distinguish between what\n"
"needs to be done, what is in progress and what is currently on hold. In case "
"you face issues with these overviews,\n"
"your Zammad admin should be able to help.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details How to get notified for ticket changes?)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:24
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Adjust the [notification settings in your "
"profile](manage-profile#notifications). You can distinguish between the\n"
"action (e.g. ticket creation), the notification channel (email and/or "
"browser), your relation to the ticket (e.g. if\n"
"you are the owner) and limit the notifications to a specific group.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details Why is the ticket open again? I closed it already!)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:30
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Depending on the settings of your Zammad instance, the reasons can "
"differ. But usually the reason is that a customer\n"
"replied to the ticket after it was set to closed. Another reason could be "
"that a colleague re-opened it. If you can't\n"
"see an article which fits to the description, you can take a look at the "
"ticket history to find out more. Do so by\n"
"opening the ::a:: menu in the ticket sidebar tab and select **History**.\n"
"\n"
"Your Zammad admin can adjust what should happen when a customer replies "
"after a ticket got closed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details What does the customer see in the ticket?)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By default, customers only have a reduced interface. They can create "
"tickets, view their own tickets (and maybe their\n"
"colleague's too, depending on the setting) and access their profile "
"settings. Even the ticket detail view only includes\n"
"relevant elements for the customer. Elements, which have an internal purpose "
"(like group, priority, internal notes, are\n"
"not visible to the customer.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details What does the customer see in the ticket?|warning)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The explanation above is based on the default Zammad settings. Be aware that "
"the configuration of your system might be\n"
"different. If in doubt, you should ask your admin.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details I can't log in. What can I do?)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:51
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"- Forgot your password? Try resetting it in the login screen under the "
"**Forgot password?** link by providing your email\n"
"  address.\n"
"- Lost the possibility to provide your 2nd factor for "
"2-factor-authentication (2FA)? Use a recovery code and set up a\n"
"  new 2FA method. See [2FA page](./guides/two-factor-auth) for more "
"information.\n"
"- Lost your 2FA recovery codes? Get in touch with your Zammad admin. This "
"also applies if your problem is not mentioned\n"
"  here.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details How can I use keyboard shortcuts? I want to be more productive.)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:61
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Just use them! You can find an overview of the available shortcuts by "
"pressing [[?]] on your keyboard or open the\n"
"overview from the avatar menu (click on your avatar in the bottom left "
"corner and select **Keyboard shortcuts**).\n"
"\n"
"Some of them depend on the location you are or action you perform "
"(e.g. being in the editor or in the ticket\n"
"detail view).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details How to switch between dark and light mode for the user interface?)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:69
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can switch between light, dark and automatic mode (tries to adapt to "
"your browser) in the avatar menu. Open it\n"
"by clicking your avatar in the bottom left corner and switch the toggle to "
"the desired state.\n"
"\n"
"Another possibility is to use the keyboard shortcut [[d]]. If no input field "
"is activated, pressing it cycles between\n"
"the different modes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:77
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "User Profile"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details How to change my profile/avatar image?)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:79
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Go to the [avatar section in you profile settings](manage-profile#avatar) by "
"opening the avatar menu in the bottom\n"
"left corner and select **Profile settings**. There you can upload an image, "
"capture a photo (if your device has a\n"
"camera) or delete already present images.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details I want to change the language of the Zammad user interface. How can I do that?)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:85
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Go to the language section in you profile settings by opening the avatar "
"menu in the bottom left corner and select\n"
"**Profile settings**.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details What should I do before going on vacation?)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:90
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Go to the [out of office section](manage-profile#out-of-office) in you "
"profile settings by opening the avatar menu in\n"
"the bottom left corner and select **Profile settings**. There you can define "
"a replacement agent.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details Can I adjust the order of the overviews?)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:95
#, no-wrap
msgid "Yes! Read on [here](guides/overviews#reorder-overviews).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:99
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Work on Tickets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details How to assign somebody to a ticket?)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:101
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the ticket sidebar tab, you can find an **Owner** field. Choose from the "
"offered agents and make sure to leave an\n"
"internal note so the other agent knows what it is about.\n"
"\n"
"If you only have a question or need some information, you could also just\n"
"[mention a colleague](advanced-features#mention-a-colleague) in an article "
"by using `@@` and raise your question.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details How to delete a ticket?)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:109
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First of all, tickets can't be deleted by agents. This is done for the "
"reason of transparency and to prevent deletion\n"
"by accident and arbitrary deletion.\n"
"\n"
"However, if customers want their data to be deleted (e.g. due to a GDPR "
"deletion request), this can be done in Zammad.\n"
"Contact your Zammad admin and ask to execute the deletion job.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details How to use text templates?)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:117
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use Zammad's [text modules](advanced-features#use-text-modules) by typing "
"`::` in the article editor. If you need to\n"
"have additional modules, ask your Zammad admin to add it for you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details How to ask a colleague for help in the ticket?)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Either [mention a colleague](advanced-features#mention-a-colleague) in an "
"article by using `@@` and raise your question.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details How to cite the customer's email or parts of it?)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:126
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To partially or selective cite the article or parts of it, mark the text, "
"you want to cite, and click on the **Reply**\n"
"button next to the article. This can be done even multiple times (e.g. to "
"answer different parts of the ticket).\n"
"\n"
"The citation of the whole article depends on how your Zammad is "
"configured. If you want to apply changes to this\n"
"behavior, ask your admin to change it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: src/en/documentation/use/general.md:6 src/en/documentation/use/index.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Use Zammad"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/general.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Welcome to the user documentation of Zammad. Here you can learn how to use "
"Zammad to collaborate with your colleagues even better!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/general.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In general, Zammad should be pretty self explanatory. However, there are "
"features that are not obvious at first glance.  These features are described "
"in this documentation as well as some general explanations and tips."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/general.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This documentation is divided into different sections. Currently you are "
"viewing the _General_ section in the\n"
"_Documentation > Use Zammad_ section. Use the left sidebar to navigate to "
"your desired information or the search in the\n"
"header. You can even activate the search by using the keyboard shortcut "
"[[Ctrl]] [[k]].\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/general.md:20
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Zammad Beginner"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/general.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you are new to Zammad and ticketing software at all, our recommendation "
"is to have a look at the [Start with Zammad](start-using-zammad) page. You "
"can find a description of some important UI elements there as well as basic "
"ticket attributes and how to use them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/general.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Advanced User"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/general.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you are already familiar with the basics of Zammad, you should have a "
"look at the [advanced features](advanced-features) page."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/general.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you can't find what you are looking for, try the search in the header of "
"the site."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/general.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Administrator"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/general.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Are you an administrator and want to learn how to configure and manage "
"Zammad? Then head over to the [manage "
"Zammad](/en/documentation/manage-zammad/general) section, have a look at the "
"tutorials and reference and use the search."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:1
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Zammad AI"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad is getting even smarter! We are expanding Zammad's AI capabilities to "
"help you manage support tickets even more efficiently. The initial focus is "
"on ticket summaries, but more features will arrive soon! ✨🚀"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The AI features have to be configured and activated by your "
"administrator. If you can't see it, it is not configured.\n"
"More information about how to configure and activate it can be found in the "
"admin section.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket Summary"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The ticket summary feature does what it says: it summarizes the ticket's "
"content. This can be a huge time saver when dealing with large tickets "
"and/or many hand-overs between agents."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If the feature is activated, a banner is shown below the articles in the "
"ticket detail view. By clicking the `See Summary` button, the **Summary** "
"sidebar tab is opened and you can read the summary. The summary is created "
"when you open a ticket."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows Zammad's ticket detail view with highlighted ticket "
"summary banner and summary "
"sidebar](/screenshots/cypress/usage-guide-ai.cy.js/ai-ticket-summary-sidebar.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Depending on the configuration of your Zammad instance, the summary includes "
"the following sections:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "Customer intent"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "Conversation summary"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open questions (optional)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "Suggested next steps (optional)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If suggested next steps and the checklist feature are activated, you can "
"even add single items or all the suggested next steps to a "
"[checklist](../advanced-features#checklists) to keep track of the open tasks "
"in this ticket."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you don't want to see the banner below the articles, you can permanently "
"hide it. To get the banner again, go to **Appearance** in your [profile "
"settings](../manage-profile) and re-activate it by toggling the checkbox."
msgstr ""

