msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In the left navigation sidebar, you can find an avatar icon in the bottom "
"left corner. This icon can display your profile picture or your initials."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Clicking on this icon opens a menu where you can find different things:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows user menu "
"popover](/screenshots/cypress/user-profile.cy.js/user-menu-popover.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Appearance** with toggle to switch between dark and light mode (or based "
"on your web browser)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Keyboard shortcuts**: opens a popup where you can see the available "
"keyboard shortcuts. You can open this popup by pressing the [[?]] button on "
"your keyboard as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Profile settings**: opens your profile settings where you can adjust your "
"avatar, password, notification settings and much more, see next section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Profile Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In your profile settings, you can adjust things concerning your account and "
"your personal settings. Some of the options may not be available for you, "
"depending on how your system is configured and your permissions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Appearance"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Change the appearance of Zammad. Available options:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "Dark mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "Light mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "Sync with computer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The last option tries to detect your browser's preference. It depends on "
"your web browser. If it doesn't work, you can choose one of the other "
"options."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:44
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you want to switch quickly between dark and light mode, you can also "
"use\n"
"the toggle in the [avatar menu](#avatar-menu) or use the keyboard shortcut "
"by\n"
"simply pressing [[d]].\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:53
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Additionally, you can activate or deactivate if the banner for Zammad's "
"ticket summary AI feature is shown below the articles in the ticket detail "
"view. This option is only available, if the feature is configured by your "
"admin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:54
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Language"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:57
#, markdown-text
msgid "Choose your preferred language of Zammad."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:58
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Avatar"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:63
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In this section, you can adjust your avatar image. By default, the initials "
"of your user are displayed on a colored background. If you want to add an "
"image, simply upload one or use your camera, if you have one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:66
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After capturing or uploading an image, you can crop it. Have a look at the "
"preview at the top of the right side panel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:67
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Out of Office"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Define absence periods (e.g. for your vacation), and designate a substitute "
"to handle your tickets while you are away."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:76
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Your designated substitute will receive updates on new tickets and changes "
"to existing ones while you're away. Additionally, your custom overviews are "
"available for this agent to keep track of your tickets. You receive "
"notifications while you are absent, too."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:77
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Password"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:81
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Change the password of your account. Update it by entering your old "
"password, the new password and confirm the new one by entering it again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:82
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Two-factor Authentication"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:87
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Set up a two-factor authentication (2FA) to increase the security of your "
"account. Your admin must have activated at least one 2FA method. It may be "
"even enforced to use a 2FA method by your admin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:91
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After following the [2FA guide](./guides/two-factor-auth), you have to "
"provide your second factor at the next login. If you can't provide your "
"configured 2FA method, contact your admin who can reset it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:92
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Devices"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:97
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Here you can find a list of all devices logged into your Zammad account.  If "
"necessary, you can revoke the access by clicking the delete icon in the "
"\"Actions\" column."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:98
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Token Access"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:103
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Generate a personal access token for a third party application to access the "
"Zammad API. After clicking the **New Personal Access Token** button, you can "
"set a name, an expiration date and configure the permissions for this token."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:104
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:68
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:105
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Notifications"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "Adjust the notifications you get. You can adjust:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:114
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For which ticket actions you get notified (e.g. for new tickets, for "
"escalated tickets)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:114
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For which ticket you get notified based on the assignment and your relation "
"to it (e.g. only yours, not assigned, subscribed tickets)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:114
#, markdown-text
msgid "On which way you get notified (only in browser or additionally via email)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:114
#, markdown-text
msgid "For tickets in which group you get notified"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:116
#, markdown-text
msgid "Additionally, you can select a notification sound or disable the sound."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:117
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To get notified via sound and notification on your operating system, you "
"have\n"
"to allow Zammad to send you notifications. This is requested when Zammad "
"wants\n"
"to send you a notification the first time.\n"
"\n"
"If you refused it and want to allow it now, it depends on your browser on "
"how\n"
"to do that. Usually there is an icon in the address bar where you can "
"adjust\n"
"the permissions of the site.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:131
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Change the order of overviews for your account. Simply drag & drop them by "
"clicking the handles on the left side."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:134
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If your admin changes the order, your custom order remains. You can switch "
"back to your admin's order by clicking the `Reset Overview Order` button."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:135
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/calendar.md:1
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/calendar.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Calendar"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:139
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad allows you to subscribe to a calender feed (ical) to see tickets in "
"your favorite calendar application."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:142
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use either the upper \"Combined subscription URL\" to subscribe to all "
"tickets or the lower \"Direct subscription URL\". With the later one, you "
"can define which tickets based on ticket states and assignment you want to "
"include."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:1
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Start with Zammad"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:8
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "User Interface"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The user interface (UI) of Zammad is designed to provide an intuitive "
"experience for users. It is built around the concept of simplicity, clarity, "
"and accessibility."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"There are basic modular components for different features to keep the UI "
"consistent. These components are described in the section [Main UI "
"Elements](#main-ui-elements) as well as [Navigating](#navigating) below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Depending on the currently opened screen, there are interactive components, "
"such as tooltips and a contextual help. Use them wherever needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In any case, the UI is based on common software design principles and is "
"mostly self explanatory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:23
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Main UI Elements"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows a ticket detail "
"view](/screenshots/cypress/zammad-ui.cy.js/zammad-ui-full.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The screenshot above shows a ticket detail view in Zammad. Read on for a "
"description of the different main elements of Zammad."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Navigation sidebar\n"
": This is the left sidebar which includes the search, notifications, "
"overviews, ticket tabs, your avatar and the ticket\n"
"  create button.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Navigation tab\n"
": Each item of the navigation sidebar is called navigation tab. Depending on "
"the content, it can be a ticket tab (with\n"
"  the ticket detail view) or the overview tab which opens the list of "
"available overviews.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:41
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Ticket detail view\n"
": This is where you handle your customer requests. It is located in the "
"middle of the screen if a ticket tab is\n"
"  selected in the navigation sidebar.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:45
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sidebar\n"
": This is the right sidebar in the ticket detail view. It contains sidebar "
"tabs like customers and checklists and\n"
"  displays the currently selected tab.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:50
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sidebar tabs\n"
": On the right side of the sidebar, you can find small icons to switch "
"between the different tabs. The availability of\n"
"  these tabs depends on your system configuration, your permissions and the "
"ticket attributes (e.g. if the ticket\n"
"  customer has an assigned organization).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:54
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Active sidebar\n"
": The selected sidebar tab. Displays the content of the tab. It can show "
"things like customer sidebar, organization\n"
"  sidebar, checklist sidebar and more.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:55
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Navigating"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The navigation sidebar is your central place to access all main parts of "
"Zammad. It includes:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:68
#, markdown-text
msgid "Search bar"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:68
#, markdown-text
msgid "Overview section"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:68
#, markdown-text
msgid "Chat (if activated)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:68
#, markdown-text
msgid "Phone (if activated)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:68
#, markdown-text
msgid "Ticket tabs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:68
#, markdown-text
msgid "Avatar with menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:68
#, markdown-text
msgid "Settings (if you have permissions)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:68
#, markdown-text
msgid "Ticket create button"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The main navigation in Zammad is done in this sidebar. It is always visible "
"and you can switch between ticket, overviews and the search, for example."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:74
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad immediately saves your current work progress, so you can easily "
"switch between the different areas of Zammad and you don't have to be afraid "
"of loosing any data like a not yet sent answer in a ticket."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:75
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Finding Tickets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:78
#, markdown-text
msgid "There are different ways to find tickets, depending on your use case."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:79
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Via Overviews"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:84
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you search for new tickets to work on, your first look should be in the "
"overview section. You can either open it by clicking the **Overviews** "
"button in the navigation bar or use the keyboard shortcut [[o]]. You can see "
"overviews as a kind of ticket lists."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:88
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"By default, there are some built in overviews, you can use. For example, "
"there is an overview called \"Open Tickets\".  This might be a good starting "
"point. Your Zammad admin may have created additional overviews. These are "
"based on conditions, which are basically rules, to define which ticket "
"appears in which overview."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:90
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For a detailed description, head over to the [overview usage "
"guide](/en/documentation/use/guides/overviews)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:91
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Via Search"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:96
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"However, if you search for a specific ticket which might or might not be "
"visible in the overviews, you can use the search. You can find it in the top "
"left corner in the navigation bar. Either select it via mouse or use the "
"keyboard shortcut by simply pressing [[s]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:98
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After activating the search field, you can see your last viewed items as "
"well as your last search queries."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:102
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"By entering a search term, you immediately see a preview of the search "
"results. If you press [[enter]] or click on `detailed search`, Zammad "
"displays a page with search results. There you can differentiate by object "
"type (e.g.  customer), what you are searching."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:104
#, markdown-text
msgid "Have a look at the [search guide](guides/search) for more details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:111
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Depending on the [notification "
"settings](/en/documentation/use/manage-profile#notifications) in your "
"profile, you receive updates for different ticket based events like the "
"creation or the update of a ticket. This ensures that no important change to "
"a ticket is overlooked."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:114
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can open them by clicking on the notification counter in the top left "
"corner. If there is a badge with a counter, the counter shows the number of "
"unread notifications."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:117
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"By default, you get notified when one of your tickets (means you are the "
"owner) got updated. By clicking on the link in the notification, this ticket "
"gets opened in the navigation sidebar as tab and the ticket detail view is "
"displayed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:118
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket Basics"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:124
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you're completely new to a ticket system and handled your customer "
"requests with an email client so far, you might think that a ticket system "
"is complicated. But the opposite is the case:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:131
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"All emails are now collected in Zammad (and requests from other channels "
"might be as well)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:131
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You and your colleagues can see who is working on which customer request "
"(\"ticket\")."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:131
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The state of each request as well as the history (who did what?) is "
"transparent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:131
#, markdown-text
msgid "There is no duplicate work and nothing gets overlooked."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:131
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can ask your colleagues directly in the ticket for help in difficult "
"cases."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:131
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"With Zammad's intuitive UI, you can focus on what matters: to resolve "
"customer issues and answer customer questions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:134
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"So, basically you can work with Zammad similar as with your email "
"client. Except that you have some additional attributes you can set in the "
"_Ticket_ sidebar tab:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:151
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**State**: reflects the current state of a ticket (mainly if a customer "
"request is resolved or not). By default, there are the following states:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:151
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**New**: State for new tickets on which no one has worked on. When updating "
"a ticket the first time, it automatically switches to _open_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:151
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Open**: State for tickets which aren't resolved yet and some work needs to "
"be done."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:151
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Pending Close**: State for tickets which are basically resolved but you "
"don't want to close immediately. This state requires you to enter a date and "
"time at which the ticket automatically switches to _closed_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:151
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Pending Reminder**: State for open tickets which you want to get reminded "
"to a certain date and time. Requires you to enter a date and time at which "
"you want to get notified. For example useful if you had a question to a "
"third party and want to make sure that this issue won't be forgotten."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:151
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Owner**: This is the person who is currently responsible for the "
"ticket. In case you need to have an information from another colleague, you "
"can either change to owner to this person or mention the person in an "
"article by typing `@@` and selecting the user. In the later case, the user "
"gets notified and is automatically subscribed to receive notifications on "
"ticket updates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:151
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Group**: This ticket attribute is useful for organizations with more than "
"one team. Depending on the permissions, you might not see the ticket after "
"changing the group and saving the changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:152
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket Detail View"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:155
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Now that you are aware about some attributes, let's have a look at the "
"ticket detail view."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:160
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The ticket detail view provides all relevant information of a ticket. As its "
"main part, all articles of the ticket are shown here. The oldest article "
"(which created the ticket) at the top, the newest at the bottom. Depending "
"on the article type, Zammad offers you different ways to react. For text "
"communication based articles, you can directly create an answer by using the "
"**reply** button below the article or use the **forward** feature."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:163
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Regardless of the customer's article type, you can always add internal "
"notes. These are useful to add information to the ticket or ask a colleague."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:164
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Updating your Ticket"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:170
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After you have done your changes like writing an answer to a customer and "
"change the state of the ticket, you can see a highlighted **Update** button "
"in the right footer. By clicking it, your changes are applied and if you "
"created an answer, it is now sent out to the customer. If you consider the "
"issue as resolved, you should set the state to _closed_ now."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:171
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/start-using-zammad.md:175
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This was a brief introduction about how to work with Zammad if you are "
"completely new to ticket systems. Knowing the basics of Zammad now, you can "
"either start working or have a look at the [advanced features "
"section](advanced-features)  to become even more productive and use the full "
"potential of Zammad. 🚀"
msgstr ""

