"common use cases. For example, you can deploy the stack with an included "
"Nginx Proxy Manager (NPM) or with disabled Postgres or Elasticsearch "
"services, in case you already have these services running."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:117
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Please see the [Docker compose scenarios "
"page](/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:119
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To adjust the stack and settings, use [Docker specific environment "
"variables](/en/reference/docker-env-vars)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:120
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How to Run Commands in the Stack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:125
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The docker entrypoint script sets up environment variables required by "
"Zammad to function properly. That is why calling `rails` or `rake` on the "
"console should be done via one of the following methods:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:127
#, markdown-text
msgid "Directly execute a specific command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:128
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Via Portainer GUI\n"
"\n"
"In your Portainer GUI, go to the container view and select the running rails "
"container from your Zammad stack. Click\n"
"on the **Exec Console** icon in the \"Quick Actions\" column.\n"
"\n"
"![Portainer console "
"execution](/screenshots/installation/portainer-exec-console.png){width=80%}\n"
"\n"
"In the \"Execute\" dialog, select the \"rails console\" entry point as you "
"can see in the screenshot:\n"
"\n"
"![Portainer execution "
"command](/screenshots/installation/portainer-execute-command.png){width=80%}\n"
"\n"
"=== Via console\n"
"\n"
"Directly execute a specific command:\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"docker compose run --rm zammad-railsserver rails r '...your rails command "
"here...'\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Run the interactive rails console to manually enter Rails commands:\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"docker compose run --rm zammad-railsserver rails c\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Via `docker exec`:\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"docker exec zammad-docker-compose-zammad-railsserver-1 /docker-entrypoint.sh "
"rails r '...your rails command here...'\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs|tip)
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:128
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you need to retrieve information from the rails server, you can, for "
"example,\n"
"place `pp` (pretty print) in front of your rails command. This leads to an\n"
"output in your terminal.\n"
msgstr ""

