#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can find the files in the [Zammad-Docker-Compose "
"repository](https://github.com/zammad/zammad-docker-compose){{target=_blank}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "General Usage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:33
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Portainer\n"
"\n"
"Follow the [general deployment guide](/en/get-started/installation/docker) "
"and apply the following changes.\n"
"\n"
"Below the \"Compose path\" field, click on the **Add file** button. This "
"opens the \"Additional paths\" section where you\n"
"can specify the scenario you want to use. Add `scenarios/{scenario you want "
"to use}.yml` and replace the last part in\n"
"`{}` brackets with the name of one of the scenario files. You can even "
"combine the scenarios by adding additional paths.\n"
"\n"
"![Portainer additional paths "
"configuration](/screenshots/installation/portainer-additional-paths.png)\n"
"\n"
"=== Docker Compose\n"
"\n"
"Follow the first 2 steps of the [general deployment "
"guide](/en/get-started/installation/docker). To start the stack with\n"
"one or more additional scenarios, use the following command for step 3 in "
"the cloned repository folder instead:\n"
"\n"
"``` sh\n"
"docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f scenarios/{scenario you want to "
"use}.yml up -d\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Replace the part in `{}` brackets with the file name of one of the scenario "
"files. You can even combine the scenarios\n"
"by adding additional files according to the example above.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Making the Stack Available via HTTPS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:63
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you set up Zammad for production use, it needs to be secured by using an "
"HTTPS connection. There are different scenarios for achieving this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:64
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add Cloudflare Tunnel"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:67
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you want to publish Zammad in a very convenient way, you can use a "
"[Cloudflare](https://www.cloudflare.com/) tunnel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:73
#, markdown-text
msgid "Use the scenario file `scenarios/add-cloudflare-tunnel.yml` for deployment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:73
#, markdown-text
msgid "Add a sub-domain to an already existing domain in your Cloudflare dashboard"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:73
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Create a tunnel for this subdomain and configure it to forward traffic to "
"your zammad-nginx service with `http://zammad-nginx:8080`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:73
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Provide your Cloudflare tunnel token to the Zammad stack by using the "
"environment variable `CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:74
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add Nginx Proxy Manager"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:80
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A very common setup of publishing web services is to use a reverse proxy, "
"which handles the SSL termination. One common tool is the Nginx Proxy "
"Manager (NPM), which can be configured via UI quite simply. If you don't "
"have a reverse proxy already, this might be a useful scenario for you. If "
"you already have a running reverse proxy, head over to the next section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:85
#, markdown-text
msgid "Use the scenario file `scenarios/add-nginx-proxy-manager.yml` for deployment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:85
#, markdown-text
msgid "Provide your FQDN for Zammad by using the environment variable `ZAMMAD_FQDN`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:85
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Configure your DNS. The chosen Zammad FQDN should point to the IP address of "
"the NPM host"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:85
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Configure a new proxy host in your NPM and follow the steps to get an SSL "
"certificate"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:86
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add External Docker Network to Nginx"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:91
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you already have a reverse proxy which takes care about the SSL "
"termination, this scenario is helpful. It adds an external docker network to "
"Zammad's included Nginx service to be able to access it from a reverse proxy "
"that is not part of the Zammad stack's network."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:94
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use the scenario file `scenarios/add-external-network-to-nginx.yml` for "
"deployment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:94
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Provide the name of your external network by using the environment variable "
"`ZAMMAD_NGINX_EXTERNAL_NETWORK`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:95
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Using External Services"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:97
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Disable Elasticsearch Service"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:101
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Do you have an Elasticsearch instance already running and want to use it for "
"Zammad, too? Then you can disable the Elasticsearch service in the Zammad "
"stack to save resources."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:111
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use the scenario file `scenarios/disable-elasticsearch-service.yml` for "
"deployment - this will turn off the built-in service for Elasticsearch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:111
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use the following environment variables to provide information about the "
"connection to your existing Elasticsearch instance:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:111
#, markdown-text
msgid "`ELASTICSEARCH_SCHEMA`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:111
#, markdown-text
msgid "`ELASTICSEARCH_HOST`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:111
#, markdown-text
msgid "`ELASTICSEARCH_PORT`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:111
#, markdown-text
msgid "`ELASTICSEARCH_USER`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:111
#, markdown-text
msgid "`ELASTICSEARCH_PASS`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:112
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Making Services Externally Available"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:116
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"These scenarios are meant to connect from external applications to Zammad "
"services. Depending on where your external service is hosted, you can use "
"one of the following scenarios."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (danger)
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:117
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"When exposing Elasticsearch outside the stack, make sure to set the variable "
"`ELASTICSEARCH_PASS` to a custom value\n"
"first! Otherwise this is a big security issue because the Elasticsearch "
"index contains most of Zammad's data.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:124
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"If you want to use TLS, you have to connect to Elasticsearch via reverse "
"proxy.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:130
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add External Docker Network to Elasticsearch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:135
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A common use case for this is to use a reporting/visualization tool like "
"Grafana on the same host in another stack.  Because such tools need to "
"access the Elasticsearch index, the network of the other stack has to be "
"added to Zammad's Elasticsearch container."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:138
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use the scenario file `scenarios/add-external-network-to-elasticsearch.yml` "
"for deployment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:138
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Provide the name of your external network by using the environment variable "
"`ZAMMAD_ELASTICSEARCH_EXTERNAL_NETWORK`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:139
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add Host Port to Elasticsearch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:143
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In case you want to expose the Elasticsearch service of the Zammad stack in "
"the network, you can assign a host port to the container. This is useful if "
"you need to access the Elasticsearch container from a different host."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:147
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use the scenario file `scenarios/add-hostport-to-elasticsearch.yml` for "
"deployment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:147
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The default port for Elasticsearch is `9200`. Change it to another port by "
"using the environment variable `ELASTICSEARCH_EXPOSE_HTTP_PORT`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:148
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Additional Scenarios"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:150
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Disable Backup Service"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:154
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In case you want to handle backups in a different way, you can disable the "
"built in backup service in the stack to save resources."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:156
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can do so by just using the scenario file "
"`scenarios/disable-backup-service.yml` for deployment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:157
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Other Use Cases"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:161
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Your scenario is not covered yet? Feel free to suggest your use case. We "
"plan to add more common use cases to the stack in future."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:162
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Customize the Stack Locally"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:167
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Sometimes it's necessary to apply local changes to the Zammad docker stack, "
"e.g. to include additional services. If you plan to do so, we recommend that "
"you do not change the `docker-compose.yml` file, but instead create a local "
"`docker-compose.override.yml` that includes all your modifications. Docker "
"compose will [automatically load this file and merge its changes into your "
"stack](https://docs.docker.com/compose/multiple-compose-files/merge/)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:1 src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Docker Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Find the available docker environment variables below with default values, "
"if applicable. You might also be interested in the [environment variables "
"documentation](/en/reference/env-vars)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you want to use a `.env` file, you can use the provided `.env.dist` file "
"and copy it to `.env`. That way it will be\n"
"picked up by Docker-Compose automatically and not overwritten during "
"updates.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:22
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`VERSION` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"<current stable version of "
"Zammad>\"/>\n"
": Allows customization of the Zammad image tag. Example: `6.3.1-54`.\n"
"  This default version may be increased when you update your Zammad docker\n"
"  stack. Please see the example env template for more details on this "
"variable.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`AUTOWIZARD_JSON`\n"
": This variable allows you to provide initial configuration data for your\n"
"  instance. Autowizard JSON is out of scope of this documentation, however "
"this\n"
"  example file should help.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_WEB_CONCURRENCY`\n"
": Allows spawning `n` workers to allow more simultaneous connections for\n"
"  Zammad's  web UI.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:35
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_SESSION_JOBS_CONCURRENT`\n"
": Allows spawning `n` session job workers to release pressure from "
"Zammad's\n"
"  background worker.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:39
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_PROCESS_SCHEDULED_JOBS_WORKERS`\n"
": Allows spawning `1` independent scheduled job worker to reduce pressure\n"
"  from Zammad's background worker.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_PROCESS_DELAYED_JOBS_WORKERS`\n"
": Allows spawning n delayed job workers to reduce pressure from Zammad's\n"
"  background worker.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:46
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`RAILS_TRUSTED_PROXIES` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"['127.0.0.1', "
"'::1']\"/>\n"
": By default Zammad trusts localhost proxies only.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:49
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`MEMCACHE_SERVERS` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"zammad-memcached:11211\"/>\n"
": Provide your own Memcached instance to Zammad if you already have one.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:53
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`REDIS_URL` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"redis://zammad-redis:6379\"/>\n"
": Provide your own Redis instance if you already have one. Please note "
"that\n"
"this method currently does not allow authentication.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:54
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Elasticsearch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_ENABLED` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"true\"/>\n"
": Setting this variable to false will allow you to run your Zammad without\n"
"Elasticsearch. Please note that we strongly advise against doing so.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:62
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_HOST` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"zammad-elasticsearch\"/>\n"
": Provide a host name or address to your external Elasticsearch cluster.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:65
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_PORT` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"9200\"/>\n"
": Provide a different port for Elasticsearch if needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:68
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_SCHEMA` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"http\"/>\n"
": By default, Elasticsearch is reachable via HTTP.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:72
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_NAMESPACE` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"zammad\"/>\n"
": With this name space all Zammad related indexes will be created. Change "
"this\n"
"  if you're using external clusters.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:76
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_REINDEX` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"true\"/>\n"
": By default the docker-compose will always re-index upon a restart. On "
"big\n"
"  installations, this may be troublesome.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:76
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Disabling this setting requires you to re-index your search index "
"manually\n"
"  whenever you upgrade to a new Zammad version!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:84
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_SSL_VERIFY` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"true\"/>\n"
": Allows you to let the compose scripts ignore self signed SSL "
"certificates\n"
"  for your Elasticsearch installation if needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:89
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_HOST` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"zammad-postgresql\"/>\n"
": Host name of your PostgreSQL server. Use your own if you already have "
"one.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:92
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_PORT` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"5432\"/>\n"
": Adjust the Port of your PostgreSQL server.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:95
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_USER` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"zammad\"/>\n"
": The database user for Zammad.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:98
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_PASS` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"zammad\"/>\n"
": The password of Zammads database user.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:101
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_DB` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"zammad_production\"/>\n"
": Zammads database to use.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:104
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_OPTIONS` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"?pool=50\"/>\n"
": Additional postgresql parameters to be appended to the database URI.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:107
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_DB_CREATE` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"true\"/>\n"
": By default Zammad creates the required database.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:107
#, no-wrap
msgid "  On dedicated database servers, this setting might be troublesome.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:117
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`NGINX_EXPOSE_PORT` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"8080\"/>\n"
": The port to be exposed for accessing the Zammad stack from "
"outside. Change\n"
"  this to another value if you already have an existing service listening "
"on\n"
"  this port.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:120
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`NGINX_PORT` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"8080\"/>\n"
": The internal port the nginx service will listen on.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:124
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`NGINX_SERVER_NAME` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"_\"/>\n"
": By default the Nginx container of Zammad will respond to all "
"request. You\n"
"  can provide your IP / FQDN if you want to.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:129
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`NGINX_SERVER_SCHEME` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"\\$scheme\"/>\n"
": If the Nginx container for Zammad is not the upstream server (means if "
"you\n"
"  are using another proxy in front of nginx) you might want to change "
"this.\n"
"  You can set the correct scheme `http` or `https` if needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:132
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_RAILSSERVER_HOST` <Badge type=\"info\" "
"text=\"zammad-railsserver\"/>\n"
": Host name of the rails server container.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:135
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_RAILSSERVER_PORT` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"3000\"/>\n"
": Port of Zammads rails server.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:138
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_WEBSOCKET_HOST` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"zammad-websocket\"/>\n"
": Host name of Zammads websocket server.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:140
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_WEBSOCKET_PORT` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"6042\"/>\n"
": Port of Zammad's websocket server.\n"
msgstr ""

