#. type: Title #
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Configuration via Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use these environment variables to configure Zammad's behavior at "
"runtime. You may want to have a look at the [collection of rails "
"commands](/en/reference/console) as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:12
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Please note that environment variables may be named differently for\n"
"installations based on [Docker](/en/reference/docker-env-vars) and "
"Kubernetes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Default values are tagged with a <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"badge\"/>, if "
"present.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "General Options"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`GPG_PATH`\n"
": Defines the path to the GPG installation. This is only needed if you\n"
"  installed Zammad from Source, if you want to use different versions of\n"
"  PGP on your machine or if your PGP installation differs from the\n"
"  standard installation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`RAILS_LOG_TO_STDOUT`\n"
": Print output directly to standard output instead of\n"
"  `/var/log/zammad/production.log`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  This setting can be overwritten during update on package installations.\n"
"  Use `enabled` to turn this option on only until the next update. Use\n"
"  `true` to turn it on permanently.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_SAFE_MODE`\n"
": Ignore availability of third-party services when running Zammad\n"
"  commands. Possible values: `1` or `true`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  **Be careful** when running Zammad commands on production systems in\n"
"  safe mode.\n"
"\n"
"  While it may allow an escape hatch for certain commands, it has a\n"
"  potential to break regular Zammad operations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:50
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_HTTP_TYPE`\n"
": Defines the HTTP protocol of your instance. Possible values: `http` or\n"
"  `https`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:53
#, markdown-text
msgid "`ZAMMAD_FQDN` : Defines the fully qualified domain name of the system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:54
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Network Options"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:56
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Remember to update your web server config to reflect any changes you\n"
"make here.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:63
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_BIND_IP` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"127.0.0.1\"/>\n"
": The IP address that the web server is bound to.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:66
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_RAILS_PORT` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"3000\"/>\n"
": The port that the web server is exposed on.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:69
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_WEBSOCKET_PORT` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"6042\"/>\n"
": The port that the web socket server is exposed on.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:70
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Performance Tuning"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:75
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Each of below settings comes with its own tradeoffs. There are no "
"\"recommended values\" here; the optimal configuration will depend on your "
"system's resources and typical application load."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:78
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Below settings _may_ consume all available database connections. Please "
"consider to check your database server configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (danger)
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:79
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Proceed with caution and only if you know what you are doing!\n"
"The settings below may lead to a very high load of your system and/or "
"disable\n"
"relevant parts of Zammad.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:87
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To find out how many users are currently on Zammad, you can use the rails "
"command below:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "zammad run rails r \"p Sessions.list.uniq.count\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:96
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`WEB_CONCURRENCY`\n"
": How many instances of the application server to keep open at a time.\n"
"  Increasing this can reduce loading times when too many users are on\n"
"  Zammad at once.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:101
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_SESSION_JOBS_CONCURRENT`\n"
": How many instances of the session worker to run at a time. Increasing "
"this\n"
"  can speed up background jobs (like the scheduler) when too many users are "
"on\n"
"  Zammad at once.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:104
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Generally speaking, it should only be useful to adjust this setting if\n"
"  you have more than 40 active users at a time.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:109
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_PROCESS_SCHEDULED_JOBS_WORKERS`\n"
": Allows spawning an independent process just for processing scheduled\n"
"  jobs like LDAP syncs. This can free up Zammad's background worker for\n"
"  other tasks when running tasks that take fairly long.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:111
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  Maximum number of workers: `1`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:114 src/en/reference/env-vars.md:124
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  You can disable the processing of scheduled jobs by setting\n"
"  `ZAMMAD_PROCESS_SCHEDULED_JOBS_DISABLE` (not recommended!).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:119
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_PROCESS_DELAYED_JOBS_WORKERS`\n"
": How many processes should work on delayed jobs? Increasing this _can_\n"
"  improve issues with delayed jobs stacking up in your system. You may want "
"to\n"
"  try to use `ZAMMAD_SESSION_JOBS_CONCURRENT` before though.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:121
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  Maximum number of workers: `16`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:125
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Additional Performance Adjustments"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:127
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The options listed below allow you to distribute Zammad processes over\n"
"several application nodes. Even if that's not your goal, they may\n"
"provide great benefits on bigger installations.\n"
"\n"
"Please note that distribution of processes on several nodes is out of\n"
"the scope of this documentation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:142
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`REDIS_URL`\n"
": Store your web socket connection information within Redis.\n"
"  To do so, tell Zammad where to find your Redis instance:\n"
"  `redis://your.redis.server:6379`\n"
"  If not provided, Zammad falls back to file system\n"
"  (`/opt/zammad/tmp/websocket_*`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:149
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`MEMCACHE_SERVERS`\n"
": Store your application cache files within Memcached.\n"
"  To do so, tell Zammad where to find your Memcached instance:\n"
"  `your.memcached.server:11211`\n"
"  If not provided, Zammad falls back to file system\n"
"  (`/opt/zammad/tmp/cache*`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:153
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Memcached allows you to restrict the maximum size Zammad may store as\n"
"  cache. This comes in handy in terms of performance and keeping caching\n"
"  files small. `1 GB` should be a reasonable size.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:154
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Storage Options"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:158
#, markdown-text
msgid "`S3_URL` : Allows you to provide your S3 configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:160
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  Format / example:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/env-vars.md:161
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  "
"https://key:secret@s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/zammad-storage-bucket?region=eu-central-1&force_path_style=true\n"
msgstr ""

