#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:113
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Please note that Core Workflows may restrict access to attributes or\n"
"values.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:118
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Pagination"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:122
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"As Zammad limits the number of returned objects for performance reasons, you "
"may have to use pagination at some points."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:123
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Number of returned objects:** Zammad has hard limits for the\n"
"maximum returned objects. You can't raise these limits.\n"
"\n"
"**Number of total to return objects:** Zammad does not provide a\n"
"total count of objects available for your query. This forces you to\n"
"cycle through the pages until Zammad no longer returns further\n"
"objects.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:136
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In order to use pagination you'll need two get options: `per_page` and "
"`page`. Combine them to receive 5 results from the first result page: "
"`?page=1&per_page=5` - increase page count to get more results."
msgstr ""

