"You can even use conditions like for triggers and schedulers to search via "
"API. If you don't want to build such conditions manually, you can find a "
"hint below how to quickly build a condition structure via UI and fetch it "
"for you API request."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:226
#, markdown-text
msgid "So, how do I build such a condition based request?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:236
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In Zammad, go to the admin interface and create a condition, e.g. by "
"creating a new overview or trigger. It can be inactive so you won't have any "
"unwanted actions or changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:236
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Go to the `Rails console </admin/console>`, either by using `rails c` / "
"`zammad run rails c` or adding the prefix `rails r` / `zammad run rails r` "
"in front of the commands below, depending on your setup."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:236
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Search for the created condition, adjust the following examples to your "
"needs:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:237
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"puts Overview.find_by(name: 'My test "
"overview').attributes.slice('condition').to_json\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:241
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"puts Trigger.find_by(name: 'My new test "
"trigger').attributes.slice('condition').to_json\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:246
#, markdown-text
msgid "This leads to an output like the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details Show output)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:247
#, no-wrap
msgid "<<< @/fixtures/rest-api/intro/condition-based-search.json\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:254
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use this as payload in your `POST`-Request in an endpoint search. The "
"response includes the same objects as the trigger or overview you created."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:255
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Sorting Search Results"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:258
#, markdown-text
msgid "Zammad allows you to sort your search results by field if needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:259
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`sort_by`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:263
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Append `?sort_by={row name}` to your query to sort by a specific row that "
"appears in the search result."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:264
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`order_by`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:268
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Append `?order_by={direction}` to your query to switch in between ascending "
"and descending order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:270
#, markdown-text
msgid "Directions are: `asc` and `desc`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:271
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Usually you'll want to combine both parameters in your searches -\n"
"e.g.: `?query={search string}&sort_by={row name}&order_by={direction}`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:276
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Actions On Behalf of Other Users"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:280
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Requirement:** the user used for running the query on behalf requires\n"
"`admin.user` permission.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:283
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Running API queries on behalf of other users allows you to e.g. create "
"tickets by a different user."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:286
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To do so, add a new HTTP header named `From` to your request. The value of "
"this header can be one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:290
#, markdown-text
msgid "user ID"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:290
#, markdown-text
msgid "user login"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:290
#, markdown-text
msgid "user email"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:292
#, markdown-text
msgid "`From` is available for all endpoints."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:293
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Encoding"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:298
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The API expects UTF-8 encoding. Keep in mind that especially when using URLs "
"with get options (e.g. `?query=this`) you may need to encode your URL "
"accordingly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:301
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you want to learn more about URL encoding, [this Wikipedia "
"article](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Percent-encoding) may be of help"
msgstr ""

#. type: Link reference
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:302
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[^1]: **Re**presentational **S**tate **T**ransfer - **A**pplication "
"**P**rogramming **I**nterface)"
msgstr ""

