#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:302
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Database Helper: (Re)set Password"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:310
#, markdown-text
msgid "This script is working for PostgreSQL installations only."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:310
#, markdown-text
msgid "Only local database servers are supported (script changes user)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:310
#, markdown-text
msgid "This script requires to be run as `root` or similar privileged user."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:310
#, markdown-text
msgid "Be aware that the script will automatically stop and start Zammad!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:311
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Scopes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:317
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The scope of this script are mostly package installations and especially "
"CentOS and SUSE operating systems. It might work on source code / "
"development installations as well, but this highly depends on your setup and "
"is out of scope."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:318
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Functionality"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:323
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The script will do the following actions automatically for you, depending on "
"the situation. It will ask for your confirmation before performing actions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:329
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If `database.yml` contains an empty password line, a new password will be "
"generated and set for the database user of Zammad. It will also be saved to "
"the configuration file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:329
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If `database.yml` contains a password, it will be used to set the password "
"of the Zammad database user."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:330
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

