#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:1
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Connect and Configure Elasticsearch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:10
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Connect Elasticsearch with Zammad"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:12
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set the Elasticsearch URL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "Set the Elasticsearch server address; adapt it to your scenario."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "Elasticsearch 7 / without `https`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_url', 'http://localhost:9200')\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "Elasticsearch 8 / with `https`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_url', 'https://localhost:9200')\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:28
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Set the Elasticsearch User and Password <Badge type=\"warning\" text=\"only "
"ES8\" />"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_user', 'elastic')\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_password', '<password>')\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add Certificate to Zammad <Badge type=\"warning\" text=\"only ES8\" />"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Show and copy the auto-generated certificate from Elasticsearch and add it "
"to Zammad. Make sure to copy/paste the delimiters (e.g. `-----BEGIN "
"CERTIFICATE-----`) too."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo cat /etc/elasticsearch/certs/http_ca.crt\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:50
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Go to the admin panel of Zammad and add your copied certificate under\n"
"_Settings > Security > SSL Certificates_.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Build/Rebuild the Searchindex"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:54
#, markdown-text
msgid "Without specifying CPU cores to use:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:55
#, no-wrap
msgid "zammad run rake zammad:searchindex:rebuild\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:60
#, markdown-text
msgid "With specifying CPU core to use (example 8):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:61
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:192
#, no-wrap
msgid "zammad run rake zammad:searchindex:rebuild[8]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:65
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Optional Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:70
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"We collected some useful settings you may want to apply. For further "
"information please have a look at [Elastic's "
"documentation](https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/index.html){target=_blank}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:71
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Index Namespacing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:75
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Useful when connecting multiple services or Zammad instances to a single "
"Elasticsearch server (to prevent name collisions during indexing)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:76
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_index', Socket.gethostname.downcase + "
"'_zammad')\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:80
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "File-Attachment Indexing Rules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:85
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad supports searching in file attachments, which means Elasticsearch has "
"to index those, too. Limiting such indexing can help preserve system "
"resources."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:87
#, markdown-text
msgid "Files with these extensions will not be indexed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:88
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_attachment_ignore',\\\n"
"[ '.png', '.jpg', '.jpeg', '.mpeg', '.mpg', '.mov', '.bin', '.exe', '.box', "
"'.mbox' ] )\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:94
#, markdown-text
msgid "Files larger than this size (in MB) will not be indexed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:95
#, no-wrap
msgid "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_attachment_max_size_in_mb', 50)\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:99
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Asciifold"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:104
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"By default, the [Asciifold feature of "
"Elasticsearch](https://www.elastic.co/docs/reference/text-analysis/analysis-asciifolding-tokenfilter){target=_blank} "
"is enabled. This can be useful if you deal with text which includes "
"diacritics and/or umlauts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:106
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In case you need a more exact search, you can turn it off via [rails "
"console](/en/reference/console#disable-asciifold)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:109
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Troubleshooting unsuccessful or issue not described?\n"
"\n"
"If you can't solve your issue using the provided troubleshooting steps\n"
"or can't find your particular issue described here, feel free to\n"
"[ask the community](https://community.zammad.org){target=_blank} for "
"technical\n"
"assistance.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:118
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Data Missing From the Web-UI / Search Data Missing or Incomplete"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:124
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A commonly reported issue is data missing from the Web-UI. This could be "
"tickets, articles, users or anything else [indexed by "
"Elasticsearch](/en/reference/es-indexed-attributes)  and can be caused by "
"missing or incomplete indexes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:128
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you are experiencing this issue and installed Elasticsearch according to "
"our [installation guide](/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch), please follow "
"these steps to make sure Elasticsearch is working correctly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:129
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Verify Elasticsearch is Running"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:131
#, no-wrap
msgid "systemctl status elasticsearch\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:137
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This should output something like the following, make sure it says `Active: "
