#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:1
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Firewall & SELinux"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This is just a collection of snippets which might be useful for you. Feel "
"free to skip parts and/or adapt it to your needs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:11
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "SELinux"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following commands only work on Ubuntu, Debian and CentOS. If you use "
"a\n"
"different distribution, please have a look at their documentation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo chcon -Rv --type=httpd_sys_content_t /opt/zammad/public/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo setsebool httpd_can_network_connect on -P\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo semanage fcontext -a -t httpd_sys_content_t /opt/zammad/public/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo restorecon -Rv /opt/zammad/public/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo chmod -R a+r /opt/zammad/public/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Firewall"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Ensure to open ports `80` and `443` (TCP & UDP) beside of the ports you "
"need. Below you can find a few examples for different distributions. If you "
"are using a different distribution, please have a look at their "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Please note that the examples below only cover the distribution’s default "
"firewall. It may not cover your case."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"===Ubuntu\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo ufw allow 80\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo ufw allow 443\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo ufw reload\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"===Debian\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs|info)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We’re covering `nftables` in this part - `iptables` is discouraged\n"
"starting from Debian 10 (Buster). Our example uses the `input` chain, "
"yours\n"
"may be a different one!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"Add the following lines to `/etc/nftables.conf` or your specific rule "
"file.\n"
"Ensure to add these lines to your input-chain.\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo tcp dport { http, https } accept\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo udp dport { http, https } accept\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"The result can look like the following. Keep in mind that your environment\n"
"could require different / more rules.\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"table inet filter {\n"
"   chain input {\n"
"      type filter hook input priority 0; policy drop;\n"
"      ct state established,related accept\n"
"      tcp dport ssh log accept\n"
"      tcp dport { http, https } accept\n"
"      udp dport { http, https } accept\n"
"   }\n"
"\n"
"   chain forward {\n"
"      type filter hook forward priority 0; policy accept;\n"
"   }\n"
"\n"
"   chain output {\n"
"      type filter hook output priority 0; policy accept;\n"
"   }\n"
"}\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"To load the rules, run:\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo systemctl reload nftables\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"===CenOS, RHEL, OpenSUSE, SLES\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo firewall-cmd --zone=public --add-service=http --permanent\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo firewall-cmd --zone=public --add-service=https --permanent\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo firewall-cmd --reload\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

