#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:1
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:6
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install Elasticsearch 7"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Elasticsearch is technically not required to run Zammad, but _highly_ "
"recommended."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Elasticsearch offers two versions. Currently, the versions 7 and 8 are "
"maintained. For installation instructions, you should first and foremost "
"follow [Elastic’s installation "
"documentation](https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/install-elasticsearch.html#elasticsearch-install-packages){target=_blank}.  "
"Use the dropdown in the top left corner to choose which version you want to "
"install."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"However, if you want go with Elasticsearch 7 (which is slightly easier to "
"install), you can find the consolidated installation steps below. Be aware "
"that the maintenance of version 7 might be stopped earlier than for version "
"8, which also comes with some additional security features."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:26
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are installing Elasticsearch 8 and want to follow our\n"
"[standard configuration](/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch),\n"
"make sure to copy/save the password which is shown while installing\n"
"Elasticsearch.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:35
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Ubuntu\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"apt install apt-transport-https sudo wget curl gnupg\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"echo \"deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/elasticsearch.gpg] "
"https://artifacts.elastic.co/packages/7.x/apt stable main\"| \\\n"
"  tee -a /etc/apt/sources.list.d/elastic-7.x.list > /dev/null\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"curl -fsSL https://artifacts.elastic.co/GPG-KEY-elasticsearch | \\\n"
"  gpg --dearmor | tee /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/elasticsearch.gpg> /dev/null\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"apt update\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"apt install elasticsearch\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== Debian\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"apt install apt-transport-https sudo wget curl gnupg\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"echo \"deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/elasticsearch.gpg] "
"https://artifacts.elastic.co/packages/7.x/apt stable main\"| \\\n"
"  tee -a /etc/apt/sources.list.d/elastic-7.x.list > /dev/null\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"curl -fsSL https://artifacts.elastic.co/GPG-KEY-elasticsearch | \\\n"
"  gpg --dearmor | tee /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/elasticsearch.gpg> /dev/null\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"apt update\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"apt install elasticsearch\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== OpenSUSE\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"rpm --import https://artifacts.elastic.co/GPG-KEY-elasticsearch\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"echo \"[elasticsearch-7.x]\n"
"name=Elasticsearch repository for 7.x packages\n"
"baseurl=https://artifacts.elastic.co/packages/7.x/yum\n"
"gpgcheck=1\n"
"gpgkey=https://artifacts.elastic.co/GPG-KEY-elasticsearch\n"
"enabled=1\n"
"autorefresh=1\n"
"type=rpm-md\"| tee /etc/zypp/repos.d/elasticsearch-7.x.repo\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"zypper install elasticsearch\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== CentOS\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"rpm --import https://artifacts.elastic.co/GPG-KEY-elasticsearch\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"echo \"[elasticsearch-7.x]\n"
"name=Elasticsearch repository for 7.x packages\n"
"baseurl=https://artifacts.elastic.co/packages/7.x/yum\n"
"gpgcheck=1\n"
"gpgkey=https://artifacts.elastic.co/GPG-KEY-elasticsearch\n"
"enabled=1\n"
"autorefresh=1\n"
"type=rpm-md\"| tee /etc/yum.repos.d/elasticsearch-7.x.repo\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"yum install -y elasticsearch\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== Direct Download\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:135
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Install the ingest-attachment plugin:\n"
":   ```sh\n"
"    /usr/share/elasticsearch/bin/elasticsearch-plugin install "
"ingest-attachment\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:144
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Increase Virtual Memory Map Limit:\n"
":   ```sh\n"
"    sysctl -w vm.max_map_count=262144\n"
"    ```\n"
"<!-- markdownlint-disable MD046 -->\n"
"Adjust `/etc/elasticsearch/elasticsearch.yml`:\n"
":   ```\n"
"    # /etc/elasticsearch/elasticsearch.yml\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:155
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Tickets above this size (articles + attachments + metadata)\n"
"    # may fail to be properly indexed (Default: 100mb).\n"
"    #\n"
"    # When Zammad sends tickets to Elasticsearch for indexing,\n"
"    # it bundles together all the data on each individual ticket\n"
"    # and issues a single HTTP request for it.\n"
"    # Payloads exceeding this threshold will be truncated.\n"
"    #\n"
"    # Performance may suffer if it is set too high.\n"
"    http.max_content_length: 400mb\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:165
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Allows the engine to generate larger (more complex) search queries.\n"
"    # Elasticsearch will raise an error or deprecation notice if this value "
"is\n"
"    # too low, but setting it too high can overload system\n"
"    # resources (Default: 1024).\n"
"    #\n"
"    # Available in version 6.6+ only.\n"
"    indices.query.bool.max_clause_count: 2000\n"
"    ```\n"
"<!-- markdownlint-enable MD046 -->\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:170
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Enable it by default and start it:\n"
":   ```sh\n"
"    systemctl enable elasticsearch --now\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:174
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Go on with\n"
" [connecting Elasticsearch with "
"Zammad](/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:1 src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate Zammad to New Host"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This is just a description of basic steps to perform a migration to a new "
"host. Your environment may be different so you should consider this as a "
"reference point only. If anything goes wrong, please consult the [Zammad "
"Community](https://community.zammad.org/c/trouble-running-zammad-this-is-your-place/5){target=_blank} "
"or consider [paid support "
"options](https://zammad.com/en/services/professional-services){target=_blank}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The steps described on this page are an addition to the [backup and restore "
"guide](/en/tutorials/backup-restore). They're not meant to stand alone - "
"we'll link and note this in the relevant parts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:19
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Migrating from Zammad SaaS? Skip to\n"
"[Step 7](#step-7-transfer-your-backup-files). For restoration, you've\n"
"received an attachment dump!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:25
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Note Down Your Environmental Adjustments"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you have set any environment variables or similar, make sure to backup "
"them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Install Zammad on the Destination Host"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For the easiest restoration path possible, please install the same version "
"like your origin instance. You could also consider updating the old instance "
"before migrating. The following guide assumes that you have the same version "
"of Zammad on your old and new host."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:36
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Activate Maintenance Mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:40
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This ends all agent and customer sessions. Activate it in Zammad's admin\n"
"interface under _System > Maintenance_.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:41
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Disable Your Communication Channels"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The restore script starts Zammad automatically, this may help to avoid data "
"loss and inconsistencies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:46
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 5: Stop and Disable Zammad"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:49
#, markdown-text
msgid "Make sure that no data will be changed _before_ backing up."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "systemctl disable zammad\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:58
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 6: Backup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:62
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Follow the [backup guide](/en/tutorials/backup-restore#) to create your "
"backup."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:65
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Remember if you've created a full filesystem dump or only backed up your "
"data. This will be important for the restoration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:67
#, markdown-text
msgid "If you want to go the easiest way, consider only dumping your data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:68
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 7: Transfer Your Backup Files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:74
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Save your backup files in a directory and provide the path to the `config` "
"file. Under [backup "
"configuration](/en/tutorials/backup-restore#backup-configuration) you can "
"find how to adjust the config file to your needs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:75
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 8: Restore Your Backup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:79
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Follow the [restoration guide](/en/tutorials/backup-restore#restore-backups)  "
"up to and including \"Run the Restore\" to restore the backup on the new "
"host."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:81
#, markdown-text
msgid "Make sure to stop Zammad after the restoration has finished."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:82
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 9: Run Required Maintenance Tasks After Restoring"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:86
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After successful restoration, please continue below depending if you've only "
"backed up your data or have a full filesystem dump."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:87
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Data Dump"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:89
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 9.1: Clear the cache"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:91 src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:157
#, no-wrap
msgid "zammad run rails r \"Rails.cache.clear\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:95
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Full Filesystem Dump"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:97
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This step is only needed, if one of the following points is met:\n"
"\n"
"- The source and destination Zammad versions are not the same\n"
"- The Zammad installation is not a source code installation\n"
"- The Zammad backup is not an export from our hosted setup\n"
"\n"
"Full dumps for source code installations are not covered, however,\n"
"basically the same below applies to you: You have to ensure that the\n"
"environments and application files are overwritten with the new /\n"
"correct version.\n"
"\n"
"Zammad files are distribution and version specific!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:112
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 9.1: Uninstall and Reinstall Zammad Without Resolving Dependencies"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:114
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Debian & Ubuntu\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"dpkg -r --force-depends zammad\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"apt install zammad\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== OpenSUSE\n"
"\n"
"``` sh\n"
"zypper remove -R zammad\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"zypper install zammad\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:138
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You're unsure if above is really required and a mere reinstall would be\n"
"enough? If you run a dedicated install command on for Zammad and receive\n"
"the following, you absolutely have to run above to fix your\n"
"installation.\n"
"\n"
"``` sh\n"
"root@zammad:/# apt-get update && apt install zammad\n"
"  Reading package lists... Done\n"
"  Building dependency tree\n"
"  Reading state information... Done\n"
"  zammad is already the newest version (x.x.x-xxxxxx.xxxxxx.xxx).\n"
"  0 upgraded, 0 newly installed, 0 to remove and 0 not upgraded.\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:155
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 9.2: Clear the Cache"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:161
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 9.3: Ensure Zammad is Running"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:163
#, no-wrap
msgid "systemctl status zammad\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:168
#, markdown-text
msgid "If Zammad is not running, run:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:173
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Migrated from Zammad SaaS or switching provider?\n"
"\n"
"Please make sure that your email notification channel and\n"
"FQDN configuration is correct.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:180
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 10: Apply Missing Environmental Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:184
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you've set any environmental settings please re-apply your settings now.  "
"You backed them up in [Step "
"1](#step-1-note-down-your-environmental-adjustments)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:188
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If not already done, please [install "
"Elasticsearch](/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch) now and perform the "
"steps to [connect to and configure "
"Elasticsearch](/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch) after "
"installation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:189
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 11: Re-enable Channels and Deactivate Maintenance Mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:194
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Set the previous deactivated channels back to active if you're sure "
"everything was successful. At this point Zammad will start to _change data_!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate-host.md:196
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After verifying the functionality of your channels, allow your agents and "
"customers to log in again by disabling the maintenance mode."
msgstr ""

